  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project RAHA : Report Hate - Rapporter la Haine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 6-month project focuses on combating discrimination and racism based on perceived race, nationality, colour, origin and national or ethnic origin. The project aims to address the under-reporting of racism and discrimination and remove barriers to reporting.  The project will be implemented by IOM Belgium (International Organisation for Migration) in cooperation with one Brussels police zone, namely Brussels North (BruNo), and will build on the Community Policing without Borders project. The latter project highlighted why citizens who faced alleged discrimination hesitate to file a complaint and the extent to which, as victims, they are poorly informed about the various reporting options. This project also focused very much on building trust between citizens and the police through linking activities. Those activities have made police officers more aware of the importance of dialogue and connecting communication and citizens have also been able to adjust stereotypes they had about police.</narrative>
  </description>
